{
 "text": "Hi everyone, and welcome back to the channel. Today were going to talk about something that alot of you have been asking about: how to make captions that actually look good. First of all, captions should be easy to read. That means you shouldn't put too many words on the screen at the same time, but you also shouldn't flash one word after another. Second never split a phrase in the middle. If someone says \"New York City\" or \"thank you so much.\", those words belong together. And finally, timing matters. A caption should appear when the words are spoken, and stay on screen for at least one second. Let's get started! ",
